    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2BXvYbsL5hJPxFZGv79aHKm)_\n\nFollow-up to #67. Reasons are in ADRs 0011, 0012 and 0013.\n\n- **Dashboard** (0011): `lem-dashboard` is no longer loaded. The agenda entries of `sp-splash` (the `Dashboard` buffer; there is no `sp-dashboard.el` on main, the rename PR #64 was closed unmerged) run views of `sp-agenda-views` through `sp-splash-agenda-commands`: PARA view, issue board, and a new `l` view of the coming deadlines. The per-agenda file variables are removed (thesis keeps its own). `sp-open-agenda-in-workspace` takes an optional view key.\n- **org-ql** (0011): new `q` view with `org-ql-block` blocks (next actions without a date, waiting, done in the last 7 days).\n- **org-super-agenda** (0012): no conflict with vulpea-para in mechanism, but global groups would split the PARA blocks. The mode is now on, groups are set per view, only on the Daily Agenda (`D`).\n- **org-gtd** (0013): `org-gtd-keyword-mapping` removed (org-gtd's default equals the task sequence, which holds all keywords in one sequence as org-gtd requires). Processing the inbox with org-gtd is a proposal in the ADR, not implemented.\n\n**Not verified**: nothing was run with the real packages; org-ql and org-super-agenda could not be installed in the container, and the org-gtd facts come from its GitHub source, not the installed version. After merging, check `M-x describe-variable org-gtd-keyword-mapping`, the `q` view and the `D` view.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y8ZgxDfdguwS7VT1Ascf4D)_",
